ong>C</strong>.</p><p class=\"source-transcript-subhead\"><strong><strong>Planning a presentation on nanotechnology</strong></strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">21</strong><span>Russ says that his difficulty in planning the presentation is due to</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>his lack of knowledge about the topic.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>his uncertainly about what he should try to achieve.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q21\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>the short time that he has for preparation.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">22</strong><span>Russ and his tutor agree that his approach in the presentation will be</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>to concentrate on how nanotechnology is used in one field.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>to follow the chronological development of nanotechnology.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q22\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>to show the range of applications of nanotechnology.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">23</strong><span>In connection with slides, the tutor advises Russ to</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>talk about things that he can find slides to illustrate.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>look for slides to illustrate the points he makes.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q23\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>consider omitting slides altogether.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">24</strong><span>They both agree that the best way for Russ to start his presentation is</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>to encourage the audience to talk.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>to explain what Russ intends to do.</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q24\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>to provide an example.</span></div></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"><span><strong class=\"source-question-number\">25</strong><span>What does the tutor advise Russ to do next while preparing his presentation?</span></span><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">A</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"A\"></span><span>summarise the main point he wants to make</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">B</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"B\"></span><span>read the notes he has already made</span></div><div class=\"source-option\"><label class=\"source-option-letter\">C</label><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q25\" data-luma-kind=\"radio\" data-luma-option=\"C\"></span><span>list the topics he wants to cover</span></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-g3-1","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"matching_features","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 26-30","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><p>What comments do the speakers make about each of the following aspects of Russ’s previous presentation?</p><p><em>Choose&nbsp;<strong>FIVE</strong>&nbsp;answers from the box and write the correct letter,&nbsp;<strong>A-G</strong>, next to Questions.</em></p><p><strong>Comments</strong></p><p><strong>Aspects of Russ’s previous presentation</strong></p></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"matching-dnd-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>structure</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">26</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q26\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>eye contact</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">27</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q27\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>body language</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">28</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q28\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>choice of words</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">29</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q29\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"> • <span>handouts</span><span class=\"options-drop-zone dnd-zone\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">30</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q30\" data-luma-kind=\"drop\"></span></span></div></div><div class=\"options-dnd-panel dnd-panel dnd-panel--matching\"><div class=\"dnd-panel-instruction\">Drag and drop an option to fill in each blank.</div><div class=\"dnd-cards-container\"><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"A\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">A.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">lacked a conclusion</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"B\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">B.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">useful in the future</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"C\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">C.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">not enough</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"D\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">D.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">sometimes distracting</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"E\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">E.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">showed originality</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"F\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">F.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">covered a wide range</span></div><div class=\"dnd-card\" data-luma-drag=\"G\"><span class=\"dnd-label\">G.</span><span class=\"dnd-text\">not too technical</span></div></div></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":5}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-2-audio-3.mp3"],"order_index":3},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-p4","title":"Part 4","part_number":4,"passage_text":"","audio_url":"https://ielts-listening-audio.engnovatemedia.com/12410-cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3","question_groups":[{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-g4-0","type":"source_html","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","instructions":"","sourceHeading":"Questions 31-40","sourceHtml":"<div class=\"source-question-section-content\"><div class=\"source-section-content-wrapper\"><p>Complete the notes below.</p><p>Write&nbsp;<strong>ONE WORD ONLY</strong>&nbsp;for each answer.</p><p><strong>Episodic memory</strong></p><ul><li>the ability to recall details, e.g. the time and <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">31</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q31\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;of past events</li><li>different to semantic memory – the ability to remember general information about the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">32</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q32\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, which does not involve recalling <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">33</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q33\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;information</li></ul><p><strong>Forming episodic memories involves three steps:</strong></p><p><strong>Encoding</strong></p><ul><li>involves receiving and processing information</li><li>the more <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">34</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q34\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;Given to an event, the more successfully it can be encoded</li><li>to remember a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">35</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q35\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>, it is useful to have a strategy for encoding such information</li></ul><p><strong>Consolidation</strong></p><ul><li>how memories are strengthened and stored</li><li>most effective when memories can be added to a <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">36</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q36\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;Of related information</li><li>the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">37</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q37\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;Of retrieval affects the strength of memories</li></ul><p><strong>Retrieval</strong></p><ul><li>memory retrieval often depends on using a prompt, e.g. the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">38</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q38\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;Of an object near to the place where you left your car</li></ul><p><strong>Episodic memory impairments</strong></p><ul><li>these affect people with a wide range of medical conditions</li><li>games which stimulate the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">39</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q39\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;have been found to help people with schizophrenia</li><li>children with autism may have difficulty forming episodic memories – possibly because their concept of the <span class=\"source-question-item\"><strong class=\"source-question-number\">40</strong><span data-luma-question=\"en-c13-t2-l-q40\" data-luma-kind=\"text\"></span></span>&nbsp;may be absent</li><li>memory training may help autistic children develop social skills</li></ul></div></div><div class=\"source-questions\"><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div><div class=\"source-question-item\"></div></div>","sourceQuestionCount":10}],"audio_fallbacks":["https://engnovate.com/wp-content/uploads/2023/07/cambridge-ielts-13-academic-listening-2-audio-4.mp3"],"order_index":4}],"questions":[{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-q1","part_id":"en-c13-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"races","correct_answer_variants":["races"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[1],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12365_1","order_index":1,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-q2","part_id":"en-c13-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"insurance","correct_answer_variants":["insurance"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[2],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12365_2","order_index":2,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-q3","part_id":"en-c13-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"Jerriz","correct_answer_variants":["Jerriz"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[3],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12365_3","order_index":3,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-q4","part_id":"en-c13-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"25/twenty-five","correct_answer_variants":["25","twenty-five"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[4],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12365_4","order_index":4,"points":1},{"id":"en-c13-t2-l-q5","part_id":"en-c13-t2-l-p1","group_id":"en-c13-t2-l-g1-0","question_type":"source_text","ieltsQuestionType":"note_completion","question_text":"","correct_answer":"stadium","correct_answer_variants":["stadium"],"answerCount":1,"sourceNumbers":[5],"sourceInputName":"ielts_listening_answer_12